 "summary": "Luilu territory (Lomami province), comprising here the Luputa, Kanda Kanda and Kalenda secteurs/health zones, lies far from the eastern conflict zones and has no known armed group holding territory. Luputa, the territory's main town and a large trading centre on the RN1/rail corridor near Mwene-Ditu, is under state administration with a PNC commissariat, ANR and limited FARDC presence. Kamuina Nsapu-related violence touched parts of Lomami in 2017 but faded by 2018 without lasting control. Residual insecurity consists of banditry, land and customary-succession disputes, and police abuses. Live web research was unavailable in this run (search budget exhausted), so the assessment relies on background knowledge and the default-state-presence rule, with limited confidence.",
